        @* ===================== FuelFlow ===================== *@
        <div class="mp-proj mk-ff" id="mk-proj-fuelflow" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mk-title-fuelflow" hidden>
            <div class="mk-deck" role="group" aria-roledescription="slideshow" aria-label="FuelFlow slides">
                <div class="mk-stage">

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Summary">
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">UT can fuel student focus by putting <em>real food where students already are</em>.</h4>
                        <img class="ff-logo" loading="lazy" src="/images/projects/fuelflow/logo.png" alt="FuelFlow Campus logo">
                        <div class="ff-sum">
                        <ol class="mk-scr">
                            <li><span>the situation</span><p>Students move through packed class schedules where time, cost and access make eating well hard, so many <b>skip meals</b> between classes.</p></li>
                            <li><span>the catch</span><p>Dining isn’t inside the buildings where students spend their day, healthy food is expensive for daily use, and UT has no data on how students actually eat.</p></li>
                            <li><span>the fix</span><p><b>FuelFlow</b>: smart nutrition stations in <b>6 to 8</b> academic buildings, with <b>10g+ protein</b> meals, nothing over <b>$12.50</b>, and a <b>60-second</b> checkout.</p></li>
                        </ol>
                        <figure class="ff-station"><img src="/images/projects/fuelflow/station.jpg" alt="A FuelFlow smart nutrition station inside the McCombs School of Business, stocked with ready meals and drinks, nothing over $12.50" loading="lazy"><figcaption>My concept render: a station inside McCombs</figcaption></figure>
                        </div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Author analysis", 1, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The barrier" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">Four barriers stand between students and <em>a real meal</em>.</h4>
                        <div class="mk-cards">
                            <div><i>1</i><h5>Time</h5><p>Not enough time to eat between classes.</p></div>
                            <div><i>2</i><h5>Cost</h5><p>Healthy options are too expensive to buy every day.</p></div>
                            <div><i>3</i><h5>Access</h5><p>Dining locations aren’t where students actually are.</p></div>
                            <div><i>4</i><h5>Energy</h5><p>Skipped meals mean low energy, weaker focus and lower performance.</p></div>
                        </div>
                        <p class="mk-sowhat inline"><b>Key takeaway</b>The problem isn’t that students don’t care about eating well. It’s that the day is built against it.</p>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Author analysis", 2, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The buyer" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">The buyer isn’t the student. It’s the person <em>accountable for student success</em>.</h4>
                        <div class="ff-buyer">
                            <div class="ff-persona">
                                <p class="ff-kicker">Buyer persona</p>
                                <h5>Associate Director of Student Success &amp; Wellness</h5>
                                <p class="ff-where">University of Texas at Austin</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Oversees campus wellness initiatives</li>
                                    <li>Reports to the Dean of Students</li>
                                    <li>Influences wellness program budgets</li>
                                    <li>Makes data-driven decisions</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ff-tabs" data-tabs>
                                <div class="ff-tabrow" role="tablist">
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-t="0">Goals</button>
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-t="1">Pain points</button>
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-t="2">What they value</button>
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-t="3">Top concerns</button>
                                </div>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="0"><li>Improve academic performance outcomes</li><li>Support student retention goals</li><li>Increase student engagement</li><li>Strengthen the wellness ecosystem</li></ul>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="1" hidden><li>Students skipping meals daily</li><li>Healthy food costs too high</li><li>Dining not near classrooms</li><li>Limited staffing, hard to scale wellness</li></ul>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="2" hidden><li>Measurable student impact</li><li>Scalable, low-effort solutions</li><li>Affordable, accessible resources</li><li>Operational simplicity</li></ul>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="3" hidden><li>Declining retention rates</li><li>Budget accountability pressure</li><li>Limited operational bandwidth</li><li>Programs lacking measurable ROI</li></ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Buyer persona, author analysis", 3, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The product" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">One station, <em>three wins</em>: students, administrators and operations.</h4>
                        <div class="ff-product">
                            <ul class="ff-features">
                                <li><b>Inside academic buildings</b><span>Modular stations where students already spend hours</span></li>
                                <li><b>10g+ protein</b><span>Low sugar, no seed oils, built for steady energy</span></li>
                                <li><b>Nothing over $12.50</b><span>Bulk partnerships keep weekly repeat buying affordable</span></li>
                                <li><b>60-second checkout</b><span>Dine In Dollars, credit card and mobile wallets</span></li>
                                <li><b>Smart restocking</b><span>Demand-driven inventory and monthly menu updates</span></li>
                                <li><b>For every diet</b><span>Vegan and vegetarian options included</span></li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="ff-tabs" data-tabs>
                                <div class="ff-tabrow" role="tablist">
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-t="0">Students</button>
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-t="1">UT admin</button>
                                    <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-t="2">Operations</button>
                                </div>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="0"><li>Healthy meals inside the buildings they’re already in</li><li>Clean ingredients priced for repeat weekly use</li><li>Consistent fueling for focus through long schedules</li></ul>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="1" hidden><li>Supports retention, engagement and student success metrics</li><li>Real purchase data shows campus behavior and wellness adoption</li><li>Positions UT as a leader in wellness innovation</li></ul>
                                <ul class="ff-list" data-p="2" hidden><li>Fits existing spaces, no new construction</li><li>Automated checkout reduces staffing demand</li><li>Data-driven restocking across every location</li></ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Product requirements, author analysis", 4, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Rollout" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">Plug in, stock local, and <em>scale building by building</em>.</h4>
                        <div class="mk-cards">
                            <div><i>1</i><h5>Placement</h5><p>6 to 8 high-traffic academic hubs, chosen by class density, walking patterns and peak study hours.</p></div>
                            <div><i>2</i><h5>Infrastructure</h5><p>A standard outlet and a compact footprint. No kitchen, ventilation or renovation.</p></div>
                            <div><i>3</i><h5>Vendors</h5><p>Suppliers onboarded to UT safety standards, with automated alerts before shelves run low.</p></div>
                            <div><i>4</i><h5>Payments and data</h5><p>Dine In Dollars and mobile wallets, plus a dashboard showing UT usage and demand.</p></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="ff-partners"><b>Austin-aligned partners</b><span>SnapKitchen</span><span>CookUnity</span><span>Designer Wellness</span><span>La Colombe</span><span>Premier Protein</span></div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Implementation plan and supplier criteria, author analysis", 5, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Business case" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">Each station pays for itself, and <em>30% goes back</em> to UT Dining.</h4>
                        <div class="ff-calc">
                            <div class="ff-inputs">
                                <label class="ff-label" for="ffStations">Stations on campus <b class="ff-n">8</b></label>
                                <input id="ffStations" class="ff-range" type="range" min="1" max="8" value="8">
                                <p class="ff-label">Net revenue per station, per year</p>
                                <div class="ff-seg" role="group" aria-label="Estimate">
                                    <button type="button" data-v="8000" aria-pressed="true">Low, $8K</button>
                                    <button type="button" data-v="12000" aria-pressed="false">High, $12K</button>
                                </div>
                                <p class="ff-note">No new full-time labor: checkout is automated and existing UT staff handle upkeep.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ff-out">
                                <div><span>Annual net revenue</span><b class="ff-rev">$64,000</b></div>
                                <div class="ff-back"><span>Reinvested in UT Dining (30%)</span><b class="ff-reinvest">$19,200</b></div>
                                <div class="ff-bars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Projected at $8K to $12K net revenue per station a year; author analysis", 6, 7))
                    </div>

                    <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Why it wins" hidden>
                        @Html.Raw(Top(ffSections, 0, "FuelFlow: Smart nutrition for campus"))
                        <h4 class="mk-h">It isn’t a vending machine. It’s <em>daily wellness infrastructure</em>.</h4>
                        <div class="mk-split">
                            <ul class="mk-kpis text">
                                <li><b>Embedded</b><span>Inside academic buildings, so nobody leaves a study zone to eat</span></li>
                                <li><b>Data-powered</b><span>Purchase data shows what students actually choose all week</span></li>
                                <li><b>Performance-first</b><span>Built for sustained focus, not fast-food convenience</span></li>
                                <li><b>Frictionless</b><span>Under 60 seconds to pay, with minimal staffing</span></li>
                                <li><b>Local</b><span>Austin wellness brands instead of generic vending</span></li>
                            </ul>
                            <div>
                                <p class="ff-label">How we’d measure it</p>
                                <ul class="ff-list">
                                    <li>Repeat purchases and utilization, tracked weekly</li>
                                    <li>Fewer skipped meals between classes</li>
                                    <li>Expansion decided building by building, on real demand</li>
                                </ul>
                                <p class="mk-sowhat"><b>Key takeaway</b>UT already offers counseling. FuelFlow adds the missing daily, physical touchpoint to its wellness system.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        @Html.Raw(Foot("Author analysis", 7, 7))
                    </div>

                </div>
                <div class="mk-nav-row">
                    <button type="button" class="mk-step prev" data-go="-1" aria-label="Previous slide">‹</button>
                    <div class="mk-chapters" role="group" aria-label="Jump to a slide"></div>
                    <button type="button" class="mk-step next" data-go="1" aria-label="Next slide">›</button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-info">
                <div>
                    <h3 id="mk-title-fuelflow">FuelFlow: Smart Nutrition for Campus</h3>
                    <p class="mp-proof-sub">A pitch to put affordable, high-protein meal stations inside UT’s academic buildings. Built solo for MKT 372T.</p>
